{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2137","id":5221191189,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABNzUOFQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2137","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2137.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2137.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2137","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2137/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2137/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2137/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/8dfe859d9c7576020ef6c6dadbb677f2b89e7766","number":2137,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-2089: the re-link guard's comment at line 522 names the refusal that exists","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Refs KS-2089: the re-link guard's comment at line 522 names the refusal that exists\n\n**TIER 2 (proposed): a comment in a tooling script.** Comment only: one line of `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/check-shared-relink.sh` becomes two. Not one non-comment byte moves.\n\nLinear: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-2089\n\n## Summary\n\n- **What was stale.** The comment above the registry-prefix strip in `image_name_component` said a `$NODE_IMAGE` base \"falls to the `$` refusal below\". That refusal was removed by PR 2053 (the comment at line 509 was corrected then and lines 330 to 333 annotated; line 522 was missed), and the code that refuses sits above the comment, not below.\n- **What it says now.** `$NODE_IMAGE` \"is refused later, when its name is not found in NON_JS_BASES (see base_ships_no_js_runtime above)\". That is what the code does: `base_ships_no_js_runtime` ends in `return (nm in NON_JS_BASES)` (line 503), `$NODE_IMAGE` reads as the name `$node_image`, which is no member, so the final stage reaches the `A_FAIL` arm, whose message says the base image \"is not one this guard can positively identify\".\n- **The lines, exactly.** Before (line 522 at develop `f98afb113c2d`):\n\n  ```\n        # and falls to the `$` refusal below. Bounded assumption, stated: the\n  ```\n\n  After (lines 522 and 523):\n\n  ```\n        # and is refused later, when its name is not found in NON_JS_BASES (see\n        # base_ships_no_js_runtime above). Bounded assumption, stated: the\n  ```\n- **Where this differs from the held patch.** The held patch (Spark pass, 727 B, sha256 prefix `b406b0ec5a246d39`, strictly applied at this develop) wrote the pointer as \"see image_name_component above\" on one line of about 137 characters. The comment sits inside `image_name_component`, and the membership test is in `base_ships_no_js_runtime`, so the pointer was wrong; the coordinator's flag asked for this check and allowed the wording fix and a re-wrap to the neighbours' width. Both are made here. The longest comment line in the file is 148 characters before and after; the two new lines are 77 and 72 columns.\n- **Scope.** Item 1 of KS-2089 only. Items 2 to 5 (the overbroad claim, the one-`split()` pin, the \"13 legs\" figure, the new push-refuser note) are not touched.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n\n**Touched:** 1 file, `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/check-shared-relink.sh` (+2 -1, the comment only). Base is develop `f98afb113c2d`; no open pull request touches the file (58 open PRs read at the API at 07:38Z, control path `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/start-environment.sh` returned PR 2127).\n\n**Ran** (Seat R 92nd, 2026-11-09, Apple Silicon Mac, macOS 27.2, Node v26.8.1, bash 3.2.57 from `/bin/bash`):\n- **Comment-only, proved:** with every line whose first non-blank character is `#` removed (shebang kept), the file reads identically before and after: 310 lines each, hash prefix `0cfdb717b65808cd`. Controls: the edited file plus one code line differs; plus one comment line stays identical.\n- **`bash -n` on the guard:** rc 0 before and after.\n- **The guard's own suite** (`Blockchain/Dev/scripts/__tests__/check_shared_relink_derived_claims.test.sh`): 17 passed, 0 failed before and after; the output is identical before and after. Four of its cells (`FROM $NODE_IMAGE`, `${NODE_IMAGE}`, `$NODE_IMAGE:24`, `${NODE_IMAGE:-node:24-alpine}`) read rc 1 with \"is not one this guard can positively identify\", which is the behaviour the new comment describes; a fifth plants a dollar-bearing key and shows `$NODE_IMAGE` would then be exempt.\n\n**NOT run:**\n- The four platform suites, any live stack, or the guard against the repo's real Dockerfiles: nothing executable changes.\n- Preflight legs the hook skips on this machine (see the hook block).\n\n**Migrations + config:** none.\n\n**Pre-push hook:** (quoted from the push of this head by Seat R 92nd)\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 123 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 123)`\n\n## Before this deploys\n\n- Nothing deploys: a comment. \"Deployed\" reads as \"on develop\".\n\n## Notes for the gate\n\n- Branch name `feature/ks-2089-relink-guard-comment-names-the-real-refusal`: Linear's suggested name for KS-2089 carries another ticket's key.\n- KS-2089 stays open (`Refs`): items 2 to 5 are untouched.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T08:48:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T23:04:04Z","closed_at":"2026-11-12T23:04:04Z","merged_at":"2026-11-12T23:04:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"1928666e906eee117399f863a02ce6bb55af9dc6","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-2089-relink-guard-comment-names-the-real-refusal","ref":"feature/ks-2089-relink-guard-comment-names-the-real-refusal","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/events{/privacy}","rece